    "narrative": "With the 2026 season winding down, the Zurich Zebras are operating with limited exposure today as the majority of our high-upside core\u2014including **Yordan Alvarez**, **Trea Turner**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, and **Caleb Durbin**\u2014are on scheduled off-days, rendering our roster depth thinner than usual. Given the scarcity of stolen base threats available today, **Christian Yelich** earns the highest score of our active starters at 57.94. While he faces a challenging platoon disadvantage against the lefty Ray, the opposing xERA of 4.98 provides enough of a cushion to justify his presence in the UTIL slot. His ability to navigate high-volume usage against mediocre pitching makes him our most reliable asset for maintaining offensive floor today.\n\n**Junior Caminero** occupies the second spot in our effective ranking with a score of 56.69. He faces a stiff test in Cole (3.54 xERA), which suppresses his ceiling, but his anchor position at #3 in the order and a slight dynamic platoon bump (+4%) keep him firmly in the active lineup. **Chase Meidroth** rounds out the starters at 49.72; his value is strictly driven by the lead-off role, which provides a high-leverage opportunity to accrue runs despite the moderate threat posed by Messick. While we are missing the stolen base profiles of **Lars Nootbaar**, **Hector Rodriguez**, or the speed-demon **Casey Schmitt**, we must be judicious with our game caps. None of our reserves, including **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand**, **Colt Keith**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Josh Smith**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Carson Benge**, **Pedro Ramirez**, **Luis Pena**, or **Jacob Gonzalez**, showed a favorable enough matchup profile to warrant a start over our current trio, leading to a conservative approach to preserve our remaining season-long potential.",
